From 7e55e4a119cb1f9972bc42598755e46ea291f617 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Reategui Solis <reateguisolisjm@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Jun 2026 15:49:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] GSMPhone: retry BASEBAND_VERSION and IMEI on
 EVENT_RADIO_ON

MTK RIL returns GENERIC_FAILURE for any AT command when radioState is
RADIO_STATE_UNAVAILABLE (0). The initial EVENT_RADIO_AVAILABLE fires
before the modem has advanced its radio state, so getBasebandVersion()
and getIMEI() fail silently and are never retried.

On EVENT_RADIO_ON (radio state >= SIM_NOT_READY), retry these requests
if they have not yet succeeded. This handles the race between the
framework connecting to rild and the modem state advancing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I016db932dfe1482642dca32f4c86dc7c384eb02c
---
 .../com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GSMPhone.java   | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GSMPhone.java b/telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GSMPhone.java
index 432c59687d0..b81c106268c 100644
--- a/telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GSMPhone.java
+++ b/telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/gsm/GSMPhone.java
@@ -1170,6 +1170,16 @@ public class GSMPhone extends PhoneBase {
             break;
 
             case EVENT_RADIO_ON:
+                // MTK RIL returns GENERIC_FAILURE for any AT command while
+                // radioState=0 (UNAVAILABLE). By the time EVENT_RADIO_ON fires
+                // the radio is available, so retry if the initial requests failed.
+                if (TextUtils.isEmpty(SystemProperties.get(PROPERTY_BASEBAND_VERSION))) {
+                    mCM.getBasebandVersion(obtainMessage(EVENT_GET_BASEBAND_VERSION_DONE));
+                }
+                if (mImei == null) {
+                    mCM.getIMEI(obtainMessage(EVENT_GET_IMEI_DONE));
+                    mCM.getIMEISV(obtainMessage(EVENT_GET_IMEISV_DONE));
+                }
             break;
 
             case EVENT_REGISTERED_TO_NETWORK:
